{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789804101722,"sessionID":"ses_f475cf997ffeoDzriM53RIK9iV","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_f836e7f569b14ddaa06a5f3b","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/tmp/opencode/dogfood/D4-ON-1/work/spec.md"},"output":"<path>/tmp/opencode/dogfood/D4-ON-1/work/spec.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # `TaskRegistry` specification (fixture crate `registry`)\n2: \n3: An in-memory registry of tasks, each with a string `id` and a string `title`,\n4: with optional persistence to a text file. Standard library only.\n5: \n6: ## API\n7: \n8: ```rust\n9: pub struct TaskRegistry { /* private */ }\n10: \n11: impl TaskRegistry {\n12:     pub fn new() -> Self;\n13: \n14:     // --- Step 1: basic storage ---\n15:     pub fn add(&mut self, id: &str, title: &str) -> Result<(), String>;\n16:     pub fn get(&self, id: &str) -> Option<String>;\n17: \n18:     // --- Step 2: listing and removal ---\n19:     pub fn list(&self) -> Vec<(String, String)>;\n20:     pub fn remove(&mut self, id: &str) -> bool;\n21: \n22:     // --- Step 3: persistence ---\n23:     pub fn save(&self, path: &std::path::Path) -> std::io::Result<()>;\n24:     pub fn load(path: &std::path::Path) -> std::io::Result<Self>;\n25: \n26:     // --- Step 4: rename + validation ---\n27:     pub fn rename(&mut self, id: &str, new_title: &str) -> Result<(), String>;\n28: }\n29: ```\n30: \n31: ## Rules\n32: \n33: - `add` fails (`Err`) when `id` is empty, when `title` is empty, or when `id`\n34:   already exists. Otherwise stores the entry.\n35: - `get` returns a clone of the title, or `None` when `id` is unknown.\n36: - `list` returns all `(id, title)` pairs sorted by `id` ascending.\n37: - `remove` deletes the entry, returning `true` when something was removed and\n38:   `false` when `id` was unknown.\n39: - `save` writes one line per entry, sorted by `id`, in the exact format\n40:   `id:title\\n`. It creates or truncates the file.\n41: - `load` reads a file written by `save` and reconstructs the registry.\n42:   A missing file is an `Err`. A malformed line (no `:` separator) is an `Err`.\n43:   Split each line at the FIRST `:` only.\n44: - `rename` fails (`Err`) when `id` is unknown or when `new_title` is empty.\n45:   Otherwise updates the title in place.\n46: - Tests never use `:` or newline characters inside ids or titles.\n47: \n48: ## Steps\n49: \n50: 1. `new` + `add` + `get`.\n51: 2. `list` + `remove`.\n52: 3. `save` + `load`.\n53: 4. `rename` (+ the validation rules above for `add`/`rename`).\n\n(End of file - total 53 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# `TaskRegistry` specification (fixture crate `registry`)\n\nAn in-memory registry of tasks, each with a string `id` and a string `title`,\nwith optional persistence to a text file. Standard library only.\n\n## API\n\n```rust\npub struct TaskRegistry { /* private */ }\n\nimpl TaskRegistry {\n    pub fn new() -> Self;\n\n    // --- Step 1: basic storage ---\n    pub fn add(&mut self, id: &str, title: &str) -> Result<(), String>;\n    pub fn get(&self, id: &str) -> Option<String>;\n\n    // --- Step 2: listing and removal ---\n    pub fn list(&self) -> Vec<(String, String)>;\n    pub fn remove(&mut self, id: &str) -> bool;","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/tmp/opencode/dogfood/D4-ON-1/work/spec.md","text":"# `TaskRegistry` specification (fixture crate `registry`)\n\nAn in-memory registry of tasks, each with a string `id` and a string `title`,\nwith optional persistence to a text file. Standard library only.\n\n## API\n\n```rust\npub struct TaskRegistry { /* private */ }\n\nimpl TaskRegistry {\n    pub fn new() -> Self;\n\n    // --- Step 1: basic storage ---\n    pub fn add(&mut self, id: &str, title: &str) -> Result<(), String>;\n    pub fn get(&self, id: &str) -> Option<String>;\n\n    // --- Step 2: listing and removal ---\n    pub fn list(&self) -> Vec<(String, String)>;\n    pub fn remove(&mut self, id: &str) -> bool;\n\n    // --- Step 3: persistence ---\n    pub fn save(&self, path: &std::path::Path) -> std::io::Result<()>;\n    pub fn load(path: &std::path::Path) -> std::io::Result<Self>;\n\n    // --- Step 4: rename + validation ---\n    pub fn rename(&mut self, id: &str, new_title: &str) -> Result<(), String>;\n}\n```\n\n## Rules\n\n- `add` fails (`Err`) when `id` is empty, when `title` is empty, or when `id`\n  already exists. Otherwise stores the entry.\n- `get` returns a clone of the title, or `None` when `id` is unknown.\n- `list` returns all `(id, title)` pairs sorted by `id` ascending.\n- `remove` deletes the entry, returning `true` when something was removed and\n  `false` when `id` was unknown.\n- `save` writes one line per entry, sorted by `id`, in the exact format\n  `id:title\\n`. It creates or truncates the file.\n- `load` reads a file written by `save` and reconstructs the registry.\n  A missing file is an `Err`. A malformed line (no `:` separator) is an `Err`.\n  Split each line at the FIRST `:` only.\n- `rename` fails (`Err`) when `id` is unknown or when `new_title` is empty.\n  Otherwise updates the title in place.\n- Tests never use `:` or newline characters inside ids or titles.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. `new` + `add` + `get`.\n2. `list` + `remove`.\n3. `save` + `load`.\n4. `rename` (+ the validation rules above for `add`/`rename`).","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":53,"totalLines":53,"truncated":false}},"title":"tmp/opencode/dogfood/D4-ON-1/work/spec.md","time":{"start":1789804101697,"end":1789804101707}},"id":"prt_0b8a34039001LAdsRGEZvPkFTc","sessionID":"ses_f475cf997ffeoDzriM53RIK9iV","messageID":"msg_0b8a307de001GSsagiNaeQk6wc"}}
